    "created_at": "2017-11-10T19:36:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-11-10T19:36:12Z",
    "body": "Sure, happy to.\r\n\r\nSo the easiest example is:\r\n\r\n  https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/blob/1db039e5b6d9d5940814e5d3f559d436066bcead/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-iframed.sub.html#L107\r\n\r\nPer the spec, the value should be a \"valid source size list\". Per the grammar that implies that at least one `<source-size-value>` should be present, and that no invalid tokens per that CSS grammar before it.\r\n\r\nThat particular test definitely has no trailing `<source-size-value>`.\r\n\r\nWPT tests mostly what Gecko implements (modulo conditions with `or` or `calc()`). The exact divergences from the spec algorithm I had to do is:\r\n\r\n * Ignore trailing tokens. Otherwise tests like the following fail:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/blob/1db039e5b6d9d5940814e5d3f559d436066bcead/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-iframed.sub.html#L44\r\n\r\n * Ignore invalid stuff between the comma separated list, otherwise tests like the following fail:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/blob/1db039e5b6d9d5940814e5d3f559d436066bcead/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-iframed.sub.html#L50\r\n\r\n * Allow no trailing `<source-size-value>`, defaulting to `100vw`. Otherwise tests like the first one I pasted fail.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
